## Responsive Design

### Breakpoints
- **Mobile**: < 768px
- **Tablet**: 768px - 1024px
- **Desktop**: > 1024px

### Hide/Show
```vue
<!-- Hide on mobile -->
<div class="hide-mobile">Desktop only</div>

<!-- Show on mobile only -->
<div class="show-mobile">Mobile only</div>

<!-- Responsive flex direction -->
<div class="d-flex flex-col-mobile">
  <!-- Column on mobile, row on desktop -->
</div>
```

---

## Best Practices

### 1. Component Structure
```vue
<template>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header">
      <h3 class="card-title text-lg font-semibold">Title</h3>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <p class="text-secondary mb-4">Content</p>
      <button class="btn btn-primary">Action</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<style scoped>
/* Only component-specific styles that can't be achieved with classes */
.custom-gradient {
  background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--color-brand-primary), var(--color-blue));
}
</style>
```

### 2. Consistency
- Use `btn` classes for all buttons
- Use `form-control` for all inputs
- Use `card` for all card containers
- Use spacing utilities (`m-*`, `p-*`, `gap-*`) instead of custom margins/paddings

### 3. Accessibility
- Always include labels for form inputs
- Use semantic HTML
- Provide `aria-label` for icon-only buttons

```vue
<button class="btn-icon" aria-label="Close">
  <i class="bx bx-x"></i>
</button>
```

---

## Migration Guide

### When updating existing components:

1. **Remove inline styles**
   - Replace with design system classes

2. **Update button classes**
   ```vue
   <!-- Before -->
   <button style="background: #0F7B6C; padding: 8px 16px;">Save</button>
   
   <!-- After -->
   <button class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
   ```

3. **Update form inputs**
   ```vue
   <!-- Before -->
   <input style="padding: 8px; border: 1px solid #ddd;">
   
   <!-- After -->
   <input class="form-control">
   ```

4. **Use spacing utilities**
   ```vue
   <!-- Before -->
   <div style="margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
   
   <!-- After -->
   <div class="my-5">
   ```

